# What the production image may hold, and nothing else. A development tool's
# files (node_modules, bundles, reports, caches, generated specs) stay out
# whatever their name: the list below lets in, it does not keep out.
*
!package.json
!bun.lock
!bunfig.toml
!tsconfig.base.json
!packages/
**/node_modules
packages/*/dist
packages/server/specs/tla/generated

# The packages production does not run. Each is left out so that its
# dependencies are left out with it (C7). `bun install --production` drops a
# devDependency, and none of these dependencies is one: packages/shell depends
# on @fairfox/polly, polly depends on ts-morph and asks for typescript and
# @stryker-mutator/api as peers, so installing the shell puts that whole
# development toolchain in the image. The shell is browser code; the image
# takes its built files at step 0b, not its source and not its dependencies.
packages/shell
packages/client
packages/cli
packages/devctl
